---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Combien de Jours Avez-Vous Besoin en Chine ? Itinerary by Trip Length";
const description = "Plan the perfect China trip. From a 3-day whirlwind to a 3-week adventure — find the itinerary that fits your timeline.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="fr">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🏙️ City Guides</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        Combien de Jours Avez-Vous Besoin en Chine ? Itinerary by Trip Length
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Plan the perfect China trip. From a 3-day whirlwind to a 3-week adventure — find the itinerary that fits your timeline.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-4">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-blue-800 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>China deserves at least 5–7 days.</strong> If you only have 3 days, stick to one city (Beijing or Shanghai). With 7–10 days, you can experience both the classic sights and a second contrasting city. Two weeks unlocks the full diversity — history, nature, food, and modern China all in one trip. Here's how to match your itinerary to your available time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#3-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🕐 3 Days: One City, Maximum Impact</a></li>
        <li><a href="#5-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🕐 5 Days: Slow Down or Add a Second City</a></li>
        <li><a href="#7-10-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🕐 7–10 Days: The Classic China Route</a></li>
        <li><a href="#10-14-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🕐 10–14 Days: Deep Dive</a></li>
        <li><a href="#14-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🕐 14+ Days: The Grand Tour</a></li>
        <li><a href="#which-city" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🏙️ Which City Fits You?</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="3-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🕐 3 Days: One City, Maximum Impact</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Three days is tight, but it's enough to fall in love with China. Pick one city and immerse yourself.</p>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Option A: Beijing</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li>Day 1: Forbidden City + Tiananmen Square + Jingshan Park sunset</li>
        <li>Day 2: Mutianyu Great Wall (half-day trip)</li>
        <li>Day 3: Temple of Heaven + Hutongs + Lama Temple</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Best for: History lovers, first-timers to Asia</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Option B: Shanghai</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li>Day 1: The Bund + Huangpu River cruise + Nanjing Road</li>
        <li>Day 2: Yu Garden + French Concession + Xintiandi</li>
        <li>Day 3: Shanghai Tower + Zhujiajiao Water Town</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Best for: Modern architecture, foodies, nightlife</p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="5-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🕐 5 Days: Slow Down or Add a Second City</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">With five days, you have breathing room. You can either go deeper in one city or add a quick second stop.</p>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Option A: Beijing Slow (5 days)</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li>Add a day for the Summer Palace and 798 Art District</li>
        <li>Take a cooking class or learn about tea culture</li>
        <li>Day trip to Chengde Mountain Resort</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Option B: Classic Duo — Beijing + Xi'an</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li>Days 1–3: Beijing (Forbidden City, Great Wall, Hutongs)</li>
        <li>Day 4: Xi'an — Terracotta Warriors, Muslim Quarter food walk</li>
        <li>Day 5: Xi'an — Ancient City Wall bike ride, Big Wild Goose Pagoda</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Best for: History buffs who want two iconic stops</p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="7-10-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🕐 7–10 Days: The Classic China Route</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Seven to ten days hits the sweet spot with three destinations.</p>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Recommended Route: Beijing → Xi'an → Shanghai</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li>Beijing (3 days): Forbidden City, Great Wall, Hutongs</li>
        <li>Xi'an (2 days): Terracotta Warriors, City Wall, food street</li>
        <li>Shanghai (3 days): The Bund, French Concession, Zhujiajiao</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Variation with Nature: Beijing → Chengdu → Shanghai</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li>Beijing (3 days): Classic sights</li>
        <li>Chengdu (3 days): Pandas at the breeding base, Qingcheng Mountain bamboo forests, tea house culture in a city park</li>
        <li>Shanghai (2 days): The Bund, skyline</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2 id="10-14-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🕐 10–14 Days: Deep Dive</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Two weeks lets you explore China's full range — from ancient capital to futuristic metropolis to natural wonder.</p>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Suggested 14-Day Route: Beijing → Xi'an → Chengdu → Shanghai</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-gray-700">
          <thead><tr class="border-b"><th class="py-2 pr-4">Day</th><th class="py-2 pr-4">City</th><th class="py-2">Highlights</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b"><td class="py-2 pr-4">1–3</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Beijing</td><td class="py-2">Forbidden City, Great Wall, Hutongs, Summer Palace</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b"><td class="py-2 pr-4">4–5</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Xi'an</td><td class="py-2">Terracotta Warriors, City Wall, Muslim food tour</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b"><td class="py-2 pr-4">6–8</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Chengdu</td><td class="py-2">Pandas, Sichuan food, Qingcheng Mountain, tea houses</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b"><td class="py-2 pr-4">9–11</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Shanghai</td><td class="py-2">The Bund, French Concession, Zhujiajiao Water Town</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">12–14</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Shanghai</td><td class="py-2">Disney (optional), Huangshan day trip, dive deeper into the city</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="14-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🕐 14+ Days: The Grand Tour</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">If you have three weeks or more, add one or more of these destinations:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
      <li><strong>Guilin/Yangshuo</strong> (3–4 days): Li River cruise, cycling through rice paddies</li>
      <li><strong>Guangzhou + Shenzhen</strong> (3–4 days): Cantonese food, Hong Kong day trip</li>
      <li><strong>Chengdu + Sichuan</strong> (5–7 days): Pandas, Jiuzhaigou, Mount Emei</li>
      <li><strong>Yunnan</strong> (6–10 days): Kunming, Dali, Lijiang, Shangri-La</li>
      <li><strong>Hong Kong</strong> (2 days): Skyline, hiking</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="which-city" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🏙️ Which City Fits You?</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-12">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-gray-700 border rounded-xl">
        <thead><tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b"><th class="p-3 font-bold">You are...</th><th class="p-3 font-bold">Choose</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b"><td class="p-3">A history buff</td><td class="p-3">Beijing or Xi'an — 3,000 years of Chinese history</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b"><td class="p-3">A foodie</td><td class="p-3">Chengdu or Guangzhou — two of China's great food capitals</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b"><td class="p-3">A modern architecture fan</td><td class="p-3">Shanghai or Shenzhen — skyline, art deco, futuristic towers</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b"><td class="p-3">A nature lover</td><td class="p-3">Add Guilin or Sichuan (Jiuzhaigou) to any itinerary</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3">Short on time</td><td class="p-3">One city is better than running through three</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="not-prose mt-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">📚 Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <a href="/fr/cities/beijing-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🏛️ <strong>Beijing Travel Guide</strong> — What to see, eat, and do</a>
        <a href="/fr/cities/shanghai-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🌆 <strong>Shanghai Travel Guide</strong> — The most foreigner-friendly city</a>
        <a href="/fr/cities/guangzhou-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🥟 <strong>Guangzhou Travel Guide</strong> — Food capital of China</a>
        <a href="/fr/cities/shenzhen-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🤖 <strong>Shenzhen Travel Guide</strong> — Tech hub next to Hong Kong</a>
        <a href="/fr/cities/chengdu-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🐼 <strong>Chengdu Travel Guide</strong> — Pandas, spicy food & slow life</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>